-- title:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data, segment 05, group 023, part 3 (heights ≈363849.3449–≈363995.1010)
-- statement:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data for the zeros of $\zeta(1/2+it)$ with $t\in[≈363849.3449,\,≈363995.1010]$: part 3 of group 023 of segment 05 of the extension from height $100000$ to $10^6$.
--
--   Each band is a list of records of the structure `RS5.Sample` from the published framework: a dyadic height $t=tn/2^{16}$, a margin $E$ and integer hint fields for the Riemann–Siegel main sum. Consecutive bands share their endpoint sample.
--
--   The data were produced by a program and are not trusted; the kernel checks them in the problems named below. The problem `RH1E6S05.part_023_3` states that every band of the part passes the kernel-evaluated sharp band checker of the framework, which certifies a sign change of Hardy's $Z(t)$ between consecutive samples of opposite sign.
-- source:
